# Normalize line endings to LF for every text file, regardless of the
# checking-out OS or a contributor's core.autocrlf setting. Without this,
# a Windows checkout (git's default core.autocrlf=true) normalizes tracked
# generated Go/TS/Rust/OpenAPI output to CRLF, while `onek build` always
# writes LF (os.WriteFile has no line-ending awareness) - `make
# check-generated`'s `git diff --exit-code` would then see a spurious
# full-file diff on every generated file on every Windows checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf
